{"seconds": 55.8, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect! **Rh8+** forces mate in 3. The sequence is:\n1. Rh8+ Kxh8\n2. Qh6+ Kg8\n3. Qg7#\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rh8+\", \"line\": [\"Rh8+\", \"Kxh8\", \"Qh6+\", \"Kg8\", \"Qg7#\"], \"motifs\": [\"attraction\", \"mate\"]}\n```\n\n**Coaching Note:**\n\nThe Black king on h7 is trapped by its own pawns on f7, g6, and h5\u2014a fatal weakness. By playing **Rh8+**, you force the king to capture (only legal move), then Qh6+ drives it to g8. Finally, Qg7 is checkmate because the king has no escape squares. The lesson: When the opponent's king lacks escape squares, look for forcing checks that progressively restrict it further. Sacrificing material for a mating attack is often the right choice.", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36", "move": "Qh6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36", "move": "Qh4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36", "move": "Rc7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36", "move": "Qg7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q2Qp/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 2 36", "move": "Qh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q3Q/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K b - - 0 36", "move": "gxh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pP2/3q3p/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K w - - 0 37", "move": "Rh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2R5/5p1k/4pPp1/3q3Q/1p6/8/1r4PP/7K b - - 0 36", "move": "Qxh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fe